            <ArticleTitle>Betatrophin--promises fading and lessons learned.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>932-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2014.11.016</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1550-4131(14)00513-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The discovery of a potent mitogen for insulin-producing pancreatic β cells, optimistically termed &quot;betatrophin,&quot; excited researchers and laypeople alike, promising a new therapeutic approach to diabetes. A recent &quot;Matters Arising&quot; report by Gusarova and colleagues (2014) places serious doubts on whether &quot;betatrophin&quot; plays any major role in β cell replication.</AbstractText>
